-- title:
--   Bounded denominators for the Atkin–Lehner translate of ⟨ e⟩ f
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a non-zero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$. Fix further an Atkin–Lehner datum $W_d$ for the pair $(M, M/p)$, that is, a natural number $R$ with $M = (M/p)\cdot R$ together with integers $a, b$ satisfying $(M/p)a - Rb = 1$ (the datum determines an invertible real matrix [`ModularForm.AtkinLehnerDatum.alGL`](def/ModularForm_AtkinLehnerDatum.html#L93), of determinant $M/p$), a unit $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ on the group $\Gamma_H(M)$ = [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup of $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry reduces into $H$. The hypothesis on $f$ is membership in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p (⊥ : Subring ℂ)`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every element $t$ of the Hecke ring `heckeRingH M H 2` (the subring generated by the range of `heckeGenH` for the empty set of excluded primes), every Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ for $(M, p)$ and every $n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of width $1$ at $\infty$ of $t f$, and likewise that of $(t f)\mid_2 W$, lie in the smallest subring of $\mathbb{C}$, i.e. are rational integers. The conclusion is that there exists a non-zero natural number $D_0$ such that for every $n$ the number $D_0 \cdot a_n\big((\langle e\rangle f)\mid_2 W_d\big)$ is integral over $\mathbb{Z}$, where $\langle e\rangle f$ is [`CuspForm.diamondLinH 2 e f`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L132) (slash by a lift `gammaLift M e` of $e$ to $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, the relevant stability condition `StableD` being available), $\mid_2 W_d$ is [`ModularForm.alSlash`](def/ModularForm_AtkinLehnerDatum.html#L141), and $a_n$ denotes the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of width $1$.
--
--   This is the algebraicity-with-bounded-denominators step for the Atkin–Lehner translate at the $M/p$-part of a diamond-operator image of a two-cusp integral weight-two cusp form: no control of the denominator's prime factors is asserted, only that a single non-zero integer clears them for all coefficients simultaneously. It feeds [`CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_integralClosure_of_coe_eq_alSlash_diamondLinH`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_integralClosure_of_coe_eq_alSlash_diamondLinH), where the resulting scaled form is placed back into a two-cusp integral set over an integral closure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_ne_zero_forall_isIntegral_mul_qExpansion_alSlash_diamondLinH.lean

